[{:db/id "q-79818/selection/54dc24f92d9676cf40c98dd97c3dc15cc3bbcfdf412e15c61d081e8b01e05990" :answer/id #uuid "dc433d10-5312-563d-becc-a0109d8b6a95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818/selection/de7c34bbf7dd79fd9a9d05e2b7f7198e40aca73b22c018b5535c8c73f5f9f490" :answer/id #uuid "77df38c8-7d9f-5803-ab98-af624a900872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818/selection/3059c5c3b79e9bcd9f04da8299c1e7a5c36f3641b73ce7df9a1459b5a078c071" :answer/id #uuid "49899034-94cb-5a11-ad00-764fc4d28636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818/selection/c27e9385eabdfce73e3b59dbd66cec7393f66c50a83dd04fb22e8c1e3f2c3905" :answer/id #uuid "b2ed86e4-a414-5de3-9213-a95cf9a298ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818/selection/25c5f95614239a85e590e8829ec5e0fcad215b9848e1b81c01590b70efafd077" :answer/id #uuid "615f7a80-72d3-5c42-b80a-6b974cb53843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d768bcb6-12f3-5ae8-820b-17273a5b7c28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79818/selection/25c5f95614239a85e590e8829ec5e0fcad215b9848e1b81c01590b70efafd077" :answer-field/choices ["q-79818/selection/54dc24f92d9676cf40c98dd97c3dc15cc3bbcfdf412e15c61d081e8b01e05990" "q-79818/selection/de7c34bbf7dd79fd9a9d05e2b7f7198e40aca73b22c018b5535c8c73f5f9f490" "q-79818/selection/3059c5c3b79e9bcd9f04da8299c1e7a5c36f3641b73ce7df9a1459b5a078c071" "q-79818/selection/c27e9385eabdfce73e3b59dbd66cec7393f66c50a83dd04fb22e8c1e3f2c3905" "q-79818/selection/25c5f95614239a85e590e8829ec5e0fcad215b9848e1b81c01590b70efafd077"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79818" :question/id #uuid "d3982d0a-beeb-54d4-840e-843a9e35c690" :question/math-academy-id "q-79818" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y={e}^{x},\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)={e}^{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79818/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c49e068-198f-59ab-8835-7018b02d7d0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection/5f56ad710afd0631384a359b0f8cf174f7ad04616659acf8b12e382f6e1bbb4f" :answer/id #uuid "810099ea-8d00-5a5c-99b9-1e4b8220fa01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection/a54e8107f9244be5fb56379b32c012bc796addc976a74b011083b8b3dbedcbcd" :answer/id #uuid "dfef8aa4-b936-5671-9dcc-21b89eeb6a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection/24144afa32fd354ae2a3ecb595b4a4e0ef05d09a6dcc906febabfe9e5ce10f70" :answer/id #uuid "5372155f-b2c5-5fec-81fe-e0ba5ccff036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot 2)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection/dc23ebad185084469584ecd7bf003f4365c1a7be3acbed7a7b60e8498f9e1275" :answer/id #uuid "2484f6b4-55e3-58f1-86db-38c1b364636d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection/57de49c4803829e4ae48ab12b79a460c01673c673d210f124e54c8301a32c06e" :answer/id #uuid "6c3a1c6c-8007-5614-8510-4ad886872f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c62660b7-88d0-59f3-b243-ef8b04326949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79819/selection/dc23ebad185084469584ecd7bf003f4365c1a7be3acbed7a7b60e8498f9e1275" :answer-field/choices ["q-79819/selection/5f56ad710afd0631384a359b0f8cf174f7ad04616659acf8b12e382f6e1bbb4f" "q-79819/selection/a54e8107f9244be5fb56379b32c012bc796addc976a74b011083b8b3dbedcbcd" "q-79819/selection/24144afa32fd354ae2a3ecb595b4a4e0ef05d09a6dcc906febabfe9e5ce10f70" "q-79819/selection/dc23ebad185084469584ecd7bf003f4365c1a7be3acbed7a7b60e8498f9e1275" "q-79819/selection/57de49c4803829e4ae48ab12b79a460c01673c673d210f124e54c8301a32c06e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79819" :question/id #uuid "6e677fdd-ff3d-5255-ae99-601ff749d3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79819" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=1\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79819/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c49e068-198f-59ab-8835-7018b02d7d0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79819"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection/198e9f1eaed9cc2284d4c9afd7932593261ec721a792aa6d17ad3f2ba7808a21" :answer/id #uuid "01925a7d-a612-52a2-b163-7ba4b20905e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}))=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection/a9b0e25ba1ca3b1b023e4a245f9db0ff5c1f7987509a7e43ffddc41ef742e194" :answer/id #uuid "8be2ed15-9600-5839-968c-3a840d4e9af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection/7b157af1dfcebd82ed43d8c67d168a658561f205bd57548764c4d969dc1bfe3b" :answer/id #uuid "e69de45f-382f-5762-af8d-637a57ac8dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{2}))=-\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection/aedb39aa29e1e50a8695218fcf0d0ee67f26202ce852b2f3c57ecf802a0419b2" :answer/id #uuid "2946ba24-6fca-5bfd-82d5-2e45c90c564e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2})={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection/68fae4cdc1cecb4bc52ae1189636ff81f71ab452a502154f7ddc1b79136bae60" :answer/id #uuid "ad657640-a582-5d2d-8c2c-930433ee7555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x/2})={e}^{x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "30071098-17b9-5305-9211-94435ca3061c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335278/selection/aedb39aa29e1e50a8695218fcf0d0ee67f26202ce852b2f3c57ecf802a0419b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335278/selection/198e9f1eaed9cc2284d4c9afd7932593261ec721a792aa6d17ad3f2ba7808a21" "q-335278/selection/a9b0e25ba1ca3b1b023e4a245f9db0ff5c1f7987509a7e43ffddc41ef742e194" "q-335278/selection/7b157af1dfcebd82ed43d8c67d168a658561f205bd57548764c4d969dc1bfe3b" "q-335278/selection/aedb39aa29e1e50a8695218fcf0d0ee67f26202ce852b2f3c57ecf802a0419b2" "q-335278/selection/68fae4cdc1cecb4bc52ae1189636ff81f71ab452a502154f7ddc1b79136bae60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335278" :question/id #uuid "a3459142-ca31-57c5-a3d6-301c55017bc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335278" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{3}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-1/2)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{2}y) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{-x/2}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x/2}) & ={e}^{-x/2}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c49e068-198f-59ab-8835-7018b02d7d0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection/537126e4feff7a71905c019678cfa8aa8679803342e0fab7332bfa0cddaaa7bd" :answer/id #uuid "78fae640-fd02-5b2f-a461-012893fe67f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection/ef4fcbad4956413ba79c07c8f55a56cd9be347ca9640576b00c4a4b735e19bc1" :answer/id #uuid "08464b2e-5100-5517-860d-5ef8fc386118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection/27c4775a2667c5fed71d1d2539ef96917cb5db3af3a8105f71bf364b4766626c" :answer/id #uuid "73486bfb-1bc2-5bb9-8f92-19ef4ccbbbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection/711af4ff87e579a1e5dc391933a3b4d58eb9f0df7c583e9f0145e932cf465bda" :answer/id #uuid "f515e366-cb44-542e-a86f-d69f33dff88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{-x})={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection/1f16421e9682dfee6c3ec443d0b6a01e689326cc0b8613840380552097d7f964" :answer/id #uuid "27193621-7db1-59b0-9c37-bc01754a95a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "559083b4-0517-552d-a76e-d2a32c8a614a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17539/selection/27c4775a2667c5fed71d1d2539ef96917cb5db3af3a8105f71bf364b4766626c" :answer-field/choices ["q-17539/selection/537126e4feff7a71905c019678cfa8aa8679803342e0fab7332bfa0cddaaa7bd" "q-17539/selection/ef4fcbad4956413ba79c07c8f55a56cd9be347ca9640576b00c4a4b735e19bc1" "q-17539/selection/27c4775a2667c5fed71d1d2539ef96917cb5db3af3a8105f71bf364b4766626c" "q-17539/selection/711af4ff87e579a1e5dc391933a3b4d58eb9f0df7c583e9f0145e932cf465bda" "q-17539/selection/1f16421e9682dfee6c3ec443d0b6a01e689326cc0b8613840380552097d7f964"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17539" :question/id #uuid "3c114cdd-b7ed-5540-974b-ac61cb7f42d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-17539" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot y) & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+y & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(yx) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17539/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c49e068-198f-59ab-8835-7018b02d7d0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection/0c706926a4059aa23f2801687327f10199788ef6a9ba60ca89fd9109a6d7078d" :answer/id #uuid "714003c3-4547-5715-867d-df3ec93fb469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2x)=2x\\cdot x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection/989665f2a6b25c51b249519c8d114d50dc299d0d1d2dafadc71e2145f49bbb43" :answer/id #uuid "44692f8f-a4b4-57f5-8e53-8d4f1430bfed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{2x})={e}^{2x}\\cdot x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection/1c51c1e56ade0a18a1ff47c7bd6c53c9c24fd3631c31ce0eb269f31f7d74f47f" :answer/id #uuid "f3d73794-ac5f-5330-8698-3da3ed86be64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(yx)=x\\cdot x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection/07e9db76ff3c6c923345c17bfc80a04302aecb70205fb9364b10bad7393c6913" :answer/id #uuid "1c729da1-b189-5a4e-94d2-64eb262f3e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\cdot x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection/794f8c39030c6e3372ae316d21284307d03012d5f772939542fdc258d901632d" :answer/id #uuid "572b46c7-a5ff-511e-86ef-a90fedc8e4f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}(y\\cdot 2)=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddcf970f-163a-5613-ba77-753afbf5f553" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17533/selection/07e9db76ff3c6c923345c17bfc80a04302aecb70205fb9364b10bad7393c6913" :answer-field/choices ["q-17533/selection/0c706926a4059aa23f2801687327f10199788ef6a9ba60ca89fd9109a6d7078d" "q-17533/selection/989665f2a6b25c51b249519c8d114d50dc299d0d1d2dafadc71e2145f49bbb43" "q-17533/selection/1c51c1e56ade0a18a1ff47c7bd6c53c9c24fd3631c31ce0eb269f31f7d74f47f" "q-17533/selection/07e9db76ff3c6c923345c17bfc80a04302aecb70205fb9364b10bad7393c6913" "q-17533/selection/794f8c39030c6e3372ae316d21284307d03012d5f772939542fdc258d901632d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17533" :question/id #uuid "4ed12697-47e6-57ab-8aa1-251a21737d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-17533" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\nx\\frac{dy}{dx}+xy={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{dy}{dx}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{e}^{x}y & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y{e}^{x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17533/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c49e068-198f-59ab-8835-7018b02d7d0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17533"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-1/232a5dada091313e16984e74d3bb5db444374b46d43b46399f9b4745bb7bd053" :answer/id #uuid "e60d8a77-b8ac-51ec-b3be-14d01efce466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-1/4b5d11a3af879659c0f735694ff5aeac05e8f6b5a57a0e944c337a978f51af3f" :answer/id #uuid "f7c6a6ae-2f50-528b-9fdc-0e62e28b9bc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-1/39df1e289bcd737ec28eb793e91a13b2832f80f4efc359f03b3c5e44f095b32b" :answer/id #uuid "d3038142-72da-511b-8701-976b54e116af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-1/83e1dec366f108d97e826ece9b4c59c92735f99bd33e3cf0aca753b8aa8aeda7" :answer/id #uuid "9a5aebf3-a934-57ce-a4b4-bd7fed1fed9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3/x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a47dd53a-2288-5a53-a659-01940e193902" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335412/field-1/39df1e289bcd737ec28eb793e91a13b2832f80f4efc359f03b3c5e44f095b32b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335412/field-1/232a5dada091313e16984e74d3bb5db444374b46d43b46399f9b4745bb7bd053" "q-335412/field-1/4b5d11a3af879659c0f735694ff5aeac05e8f6b5a57a0e944c337a978f51af3f" "q-335412/field-1/39df1e289bcd737ec28eb793e91a13b2832f80f4efc359f03b3c5e44f095b32b" "q-335412/field-1/83e1dec366f108d97e826ece9b4c59c92735f99bd33e3cf0aca753b8aa8aeda7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-2/7b83f094d4ef0e709008c1e7d9a903024575909ab5b52d3f8d62c189bf40485f" :answer/id #uuid "9873692a-25ba-5d98-8324-87d1eece533d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-2/dcf0e3dc41990c1c6a5e817395259d6557a0ef00d3e323b8f9cda396a6dd4589" :answer/id #uuid "0fd17f32-0010-522e-90b6-a1d35e059592" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-2/b26817b656aa529cfcd1eb6233a90b34db2c5dd65c208c7fa17e5bf2b96daefb" :answer/id #uuid "92073477-c596-5120-b0a4-9400a23c9489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-2/6bad374e2579013c091506df6bfa6feb7d8d6ea4e94107ee537b2650d1f69839" :answer/id #uuid "edc8939a-a96e-5d4e-b14c-ad9a4ffebdd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "22df1977-64c8-51b4-88fc-99ab6d2ef37b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335412/field-2/7b83f094d4ef0e709008c1e7d9a903024575909ab5b52d3f8d62c189bf40485f" :answer-field/choices ["q-335412/field-2/7b83f094d4ef0e709008c1e7d9a903024575909ab5b52d3f8d62c189bf40485f" "q-335412/field-2/dcf0e3dc41990c1c6a5e817395259d6557a0ef00d3e323b8f9cda396a6dd4589" "q-335412/field-2/b26817b656aa529cfcd1eb6233a90b34db2c5dd65c208c7fa17e5bf2b96daefb" "q-335412/field-2/6bad374e2579013c091506df6bfa6feb7d8d6ea4e94107ee537b2650d1f69839"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335412" :question/id #uuid "b6a5ab99-8665-59c6-9abd-475eeed72999" :question/math-academy-id "q-335412" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335412/field-1" "q-335412/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bbeb4f6-23b2-586c-8cb9-9742cce5a9a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335402/field-1/74521c50c65fc6a52056746481c6d39edacf577250ffbffd7ae5248b235295c6" :answer/id #uuid "88ccfeab-be0b-57f8-8cec-8e46e40fde65" :ans