34a59fa56e99a569ba05e7f7e2114390fc629dc72c7a4aec44a" "q-339138/field-2/bc57983add8ac05e8d4d561346f60d98e255e7b3cb90b48ad0a1a58e71b81a8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339138" :question/id #uuid "08d92346-a7e8-58c6-8d60-e4702d743dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339138" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot x{e}^{3x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339138/field-1" "q-339138/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bbeb4f6-23b2-586c-8cb9-9742cce5a9a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-1/e4569850392ac079c3ed2cea12b8962eaf083027ecdf10e478692316e875e4b6" :answer/id #uuid "f23f3fdf-48db-5642-b880-93ab3300a0db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "e7255897-ca61-51f6-b288-7f7fdab7e72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-1/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" :answer/id #uuid "ee2107ca-4041-57f0-ad4d-b4cd01d77c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-1/f46dc06ef286a91d87a27b11dd6b5e318974af516ab8aec2cc5c5cf2d25f4ee9" :answer/id #uuid "2b1e7f2d-d753-5bb8-9e4e-4771eb752644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "43dce27c-78a7-53af-a421-0d666e556457" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339140/field-1/f46dc06ef286a91d87a27b11dd6b5e318974af516ab8aec2cc5c5cf2d25f4ee9" :answer-field/choices ["q-339140/field-1/e4569850392ac079c3ed2cea12b8962eaf083027ecdf10e478692316e875e4b6" "q-339140/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" "q-339140/field-1/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" "q-339140/field-1/f46dc06ef286a91d87a27b11dd6b5e318974af516ab8aec2cc5c5cf2d25f4ee9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-2/ac49128e846689860e2436a72c4173d7f259a500451d5c9a303598fbb36797b2" :answer/id #uuid "0604db5e-3279-598b-a8bb-75de180c1f66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-2/e9e342c43309602c6d151065fb90b33544f10c5bd820750ad634c6b3ca4a7fdf" :answer/id #uuid "933c36ef-61a4-5af8-b610-00495817af98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-2/6dd05bce7631bbda42545b82ddc8027ea365f9daaf8e7a5e75b59ff4e59bbf5d" :answer/id #uuid "7894d8fa-a7a2-58bf-9b7f-522a41fe3240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-2/af6c7691b0dcd6d5377501b5ce6f0a4161bdfc546be1eaf6538dc4f1c6f25cfd" :answer/id #uuid "5c275c60-3344-5692-b4d8-92e1fbab299c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "57711109-41a9-5bd3-b179-91c5c32d4326" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339140/field-2/6dd05bce7631bbda42545b82ddc8027ea365f9daaf8e7a5e75b59ff4e59bbf5d" :answer-field/choices ["q-339140/field-2/ac49128e846689860e2436a72c4173d7f259a500451d5c9a303598fbb36797b2" "q-339140/field-2/e9e342c43309602c6d151065fb90b33544f10c5bd820750ad634c6b3ca4a7fdf" "q-339140/field-2/6dd05bce7631bbda42545b82ddc8027ea365f9daaf8e7a5e75b59ff4e59bbf5d" "q-339140/field-2/af6c7691b0dcd6d5377501b5ce6f0a4161bdfc546be1eaf6538dc4f1c6f25cfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339140" :question/id #uuid "6a456b54-b307-5f53-a533-2575ea7e31b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-339140" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=7,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=7.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot 7 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =7{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{5})\\,dx & =\\int 7{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339140/field-1" "q-339140/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bbeb4f6-23b2-586c-8cb9-9742cce5a9a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339140"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-1/712ad4d2eb81427722c94a6f49e3c68ba21558d0bc73335208c7e3d367d12131" :answer/id #uuid "83f68197-651d-55a3-a507-deabd92bdd10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "4d8fd376-f47d-57e1-9b78-1afa0129b97d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-1/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" :answer/id #uuid "2a1151cd-61da-5475-807c-fe26159414af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "db702fda-0d40-5b7e-b077-fb97944c0a52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebcbec9c-fd96-5eca-a3b3-5246f9620bf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335812/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer-field/choices ["q-335812/field-1/712ad4d2eb81427722c94a6f49e3c68ba21558d0bc73335208c7e3d367d12131" "q-335812/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" "q-335812/field-1/d8d9c5d6ea7de2690b493802e3ea12f2a2ec2c9642e45075a162a4226ac30046" "q-335812/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-2/7eda23497cdec583bce47bfd569cfa363cc7ef8e24a4e984424fe32371d5e682" :answer/id #uuid "b1a8bece-a0dc-5cb4-b7f7-779a2e18242d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-2/18f001254b951810f4ac3b5af949f3826b97082979ea5cf4878b654f0ec7a7b9" :answer/id #uuid "702a4745-95e1-5ff5-a1ff-cb59a8736923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-2/b374160c2e58aa1315bd10a5695a29c5fa7ac40f4d359d2738c3aea334e8544b" :answer/id #uuid "a231487a-3f21-58e4-9c2c-a5c7f875dbf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-2/c8208a24fda4236f35699dd9aaaef30ba334d4111dc1b0d36606e941231502b6" :answer/id #uuid "e0d09860-63bf-5a67-b06d-93874d65db92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "15b34bf6-34d7-5179-8425-1fe9b7f4ba0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335812/field-2/c8208a24fda4236f35699dd9aaaef30ba334d4111dc1b0d36606e941231502b6" :answer-field/choices ["q-335812/field-2/7eda23497cdec583bce47bfd569cfa363cc7ef8e24a4e984424fe32371d5e682" "q-335812/field-2/18f001254b951810f4ac3b5af949f3826b97082979ea5cf4878b654f0ec7a7b9" "q-335812/field-2/b374160c2e58aa1315bd10a5695a29c5fa7ac40f4d359d2738c3aea334e8544b" "q-335812/field-2/c8208a24fda4236f35699dd9aaaef30ba334d4111dc1b0d36606e941231502b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335812" :question/id #uuid "2162d333-a174-5ff0-ac6f-16de19141bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-335812" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2C}{\\pi } \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335812/field-1" "q-335812/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-1/c975509865ebe917a276e7d586e7e6792b21fdfdb264ac448a7ca14faf6d2041" :answer/id #uuid "29d11ed9-b43e-56b8-b040-a3bb95c2c6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-1/712ad4d2eb81427722c94a6f49e3c68ba21558d0bc73335208c7e3d367d12131" :answer/id #uuid "98d3da2f-c3bc-55d0-b345-aeb8df1e3b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "b51aef8b-7033-5481-96ec-98692a0f458b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-1/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer/id #uuid "4f8d4b10-d0e9-5b3b-9cd3-8daf6602f605" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcffd45-7313-58fe-b129-d00d842457aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335806/field-1/712ad4d2eb81427722c94a6f49e3c68ba21558d0bc73335208c7e3d367d12131" :answer-field/choices ["q-335806/field-1/c975509865ebe917a276e7d586e7e6792b21fdfdb264ac448a7ca14faf6d2041" "q-335806/field-1/712ad4d2eb81427722c94a6f49e3c68ba21558d0bc73335208c7e3d367d12131" "q-335806/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" "q-335806/field-1/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2/c4a55bc25f9d1f57c7c321c751a6122c0f7702a0d2171465e76b15ec6ed6eb89" :answer/id #uuid "7a627542-99dc-55e3-891b-bf7dfa7c002d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2/1db99327498d207a9260ff74b80a80104bb3fc9e6c7d6104597ede260af9cb73" :answer/id #uuid "275d1f70-bc23-53cd-ba1f-99addafe53b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2/4c622cae39b84be16926aa39ea4795c456ba8fcc68ef05b297ebbcf2281e0d03" :answer/id #uuid "5c22d022-4ede-517f-9415-efb2a7dffde1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2/73dc1d41efdd08fce544f68e7a220708eecced3e1ce68b91a10989d2ad88f486" :answer/id #uuid "6574f63e-001d-54ef-8adc-14776bffce0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2/bc701858fa24f8530349dca2f2e58a8728d30ee429fd0dba838dc6d36e629fb8" :answer/id #uuid "c179d943-d3f7-5ac9-8925-1eeaa927ee2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "460f78f1-4d35-5460-a331-1de288db6f4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335806/field-2/c4a55bc25f9d1f57c7c321c751a6122c0f7702a0d2171465e76b15ec6ed6eb89" :answer-field/choices ["q-335806/field-2/c4a55bc25f9d1f57c7c321c751a6122c0f7702a0d2171465e76b15ec6ed6eb89" "q-335806/field-2/1db99327498d207a9260ff74b80a80104bb3fc9e6c7d6104597ede260af9cb73" "q-335806/field-2/4c622cae39b84be16926aa39ea4795c456ba8fcc68ef05b297ebbcf2281e0d03" "q-335806/field-2/73dc1d41efdd08fce544f68e7a220708eecced3e1ce68b91a10989d2ad88f486" "q-335806/field-2/bc701858fa24f8530349dca2f2e58a8728d30ee429fd0dba838dc6d36e629fb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335806" :question/id #uuid "3c6ef87c-1a0b-5973-8a1d-74f719874948" :question/math-academy-id "q-335806" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335806/field-1" "q-335806/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-335810"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={1}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =1+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-1/9a4df386f60e3f75f7321e868bbf138156f7693043a8160e407710974d54f1cb" :answer/id #uuid "f5b1b308-3d12-5a98-bdcb-880bf88794cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-1/20290c612f74c25a62a8c6938cf5d22ab000f382757142ddd721cda70773c9ef" :answer/id #uuid "f2747458-9353-553b-b791-2798fc1f2012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-1/61dd582464f025653293ef4e0f5b4d4bb22c6f166cdde2aeded7b1ba7a8c38f9" :answer/id #uuid "19613cb7-4c40-5228-9a48-8c72b0865012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-1/857ff604e3435a2ba3a87cdd284e43ec807b478af64b9ffd4b9e865b5fecb259" :answer/id #uuid "8169f72e-d2fc-59f5-b86c-a67ec49a3ec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3962070-ef4c-58d1-90b0-e12083f5ee1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335829/field-1/857ff604e3435a2ba3a87cdd284e43ec807b478af64b9ffd4b9e865b5fecb259" :answer-field/choices ["q-335829/field-1/9a4df386f60e3f75f7321e868bbf138156f7693043a8160e407710974d54f1cb" "q-335829/field-1/20290c612f74c25a62a8c6938cf5d22ab000f382757142ddd721cda70773c9ef" "q-335829/field-1/61dd582464f025653293ef4e0f5b4d4bb22c6f166cdde2aeded7b1ba7a8c38f9" "q-335829/field-1/857ff604e3435a2ba3a87cdd284e43ec807b478af64b9ffd4b9e865b5fecb259"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2/ef9c8bcc5c6c0c4de2c7b433a8a67f67f8f65b622f2df7e3916c22b5d6cc296b" :answer/id #uuid "65bfd3a7-0113-52c1-9f82-ca0d3afbd56e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2/480013f548481e350f274c2a302f28b92b43bbb9a500170c6d29b91431c50188" :answer/id #uuid "6195742e-d52e-59c7-90f7-2a75e3bfd0be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2/6bb189b1888a4692aa06c9bf256ee7b291b20a42f2acb39c04b9f5af8b4d1e90" :answer/id #uuid "9654c093-21a3-595d-83b2-e94c00af40a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2/7527c1247d3c564cfeb2efd7f1de2a49f9c68d1c7174594019249b7f3c17b3c4" :answer/id #uuid "ad8cb2d8-ef69-540f-a888-125ad7ad60e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-5{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2/d1dac26779ed2009dd0e78f1404bfb08e061cede8b9859f49c1b99ae14770298" :answer/id #uuid "e04d6724-b006-55f2-947c-1ab85a347443" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8880541c-2a69-5ab1-ba95-413bd0c95b2f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335829/field-2/480013f548481e350f274c2a302f28b92b43bbb9a500170c6d29b91431c50188" :answer-field/choices ["q-335829/field-2/ef9c8bcc5c6c0c4de2c7b433a8a67f67f8f65b622f2df7e3916c22b5d6cc296b" "q-335829/field-2/480013f548481e350f274c2a302f28b92b43bbb9a500170c6d29b91431c50188" "q-335829/field-2/6bb189b1888a4692aa06c9bf256ee7b291b20a42f2acb39c04b9f5af8b4d1e90" "q-335829/field-2/7527c1247d3c564cfeb2efd7f1de2a49f9c68d1c7174594019249b7f3c17b3c4" "q-335829/field-2/d1dac26779ed2009dd0e78f1404bfb08e061cede8b9859f49c1b99ae14770298"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335829" :question/id #uuid "cba95378-fbb4-59fe-bb7c-3f501d3e7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335829" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x})+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335829/field-1" "q-335829/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335829"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-1/20290c612f74c25a62a8c6938cf5d22ab000f382757142ddd721cda70773c9ef" :answer/id #uuid "17f49f20-cf6f-5c8f-960a-51ac5d6ce52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "1dc95241-a36f-5601-a8dd-0bc86765db39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-1/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer/id #uuid "9087d1e7-4ca8-58f1-ad60-9c68a35f35f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-1/439a639854c9228d402444eff0a00303e9deef2ee760ca22240bfc82ef4da0c7" :answer/id #uuid "b3b4bf7b-8751-5a29-8836-7198f3bedcf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "652299f1-a511-508c-80ec-e69295208912" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335811/field-1/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer-field/choices ["q-335811/field-1/20290c612f74c25a62a8c6938cf5d22ab000f382757142ddd721cda70773c9ef" "q-335811/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" "q-335811/field-1/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" "q-335811/field-1/439a639854c9228d402444eff0a00303e9deef2ee760ca22240bfc82ef4da0c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-2/b7eb968f2941969d6119cbe02c7413e307f0e76762747e47b510d2b6532df24b" :answer/id #uuid "a7b26751-74e4-5cd7-be5a-091f1ceb6b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-2/3754de57ad7870136a5b23e5c83ca737a48570cbb2a9803d7bf1c241fc178564" :answer/id #uuid "638227f3-14b1-57ad-b134-5476d8e908f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-2/47ba016ae57c0a1bddb2a9a52bb5115f0e1487a545c720973cf870a61ac3a6ca" :answer/id #uuid "17e12729-0837-5aad-99c2-355eb82e5937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-2/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" :answer/id #uuid "6b5a2306-6662-526f-b179-e68ab24272ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2477d20a-77cc-5754-932f-47114458bb76" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335811/field-2/47ba016ae57c0a1bddb2a9a52bb5115f0e1487a545c720973cf870a61ac3a6ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-335811/field-2/b7eb968f2941969d6119cbe02c7413e307f0e76762747e47b510d2b6532df24b" "q-335811/field-2/3754de57ad7870136a5b23e5c83ca737a48570cbb2a9803d7bf1c241fc178564" "q-335811/field-2/47ba016ae57c0a1bddb2a9a52bb5115f0e1487a545c720973cf870a61ac3a6ca" "q-335811/field-2/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335811" :question/id #uuid "8d18710c-01b9-5959-b4f5-a38740fd2b61" :question/math-academy-id "q-335811" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2y}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\pi )=0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335811/field-1" "q-335811/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21741"] :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + 2y = 2e^{-2x}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(y I(x) \\right) = I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x) = 2$ and $Q(x) = 2e^{-2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x) = e^{2x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{e}^{2x}\\cdot y & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(y I(x)\\right){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{2x}) & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21742"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following differential equation using the method of integrating factors.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\dfrac {3} {x} y = \\dfrac{\\cos x}{x^2}, \\qquad x \\gt 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x) = \\dfrac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x) = \\dfrac{\\cos x}{x^2}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x) = x^3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}\\cdot y & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(y\\cdot I(x)\\right)$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{3}) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{3})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm d x = uv - \\int u' v\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nLet $u = x, u' = 1, v' = \\cos x,$ and $v = \\sin x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{3} & =\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21743"] :question/problem "Solve the following initial value problem using the method of integrating factors.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + 3x^2y = 9x^2, \\qquad y(0) = 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x) = 3x^2$ and $Q(x) = 9x^2.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x) = e^{x^3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 9{x}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot y & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}}) & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u = x^3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{{x}^{3}}+C \\\\ y & =3+C{e}^{-{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0) = 1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3+C{e}^{-{0}^{3}} \\\\ 1 & =3+C \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = 3 - 2e^{-x^3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
